GPS Share
onload

share data
 - if gps is on
  - post to firebase
   - localstorage user -> coordinates, current date

get data
 - if gps is on
  - get all users and latest gps node

   - if user -> currentdate >= 1 minute
      - user is disconnected / afk

    - if user -> currentdate >= 5 minutes
      - dont track user
        - change ui or remove entierly


logic
 onload
  - post my data
  - get everyones data
  - interval 10 seconds
  - rinse repeat

 display
  version 0.1:
    - if these markers already exists, remove them
    - create marker for each user and put on map
    rinse repeat

  version 0.5:
    - update each users marker dynamicly instead to prevent DOM from overheating
    how? - put each markerID in an object
         - loop object after data is updated to refresh coordinates on map




data | markers

loop data
  if markers[data.username]
      - finds object for the username we looping
      if minutespassed > 5 min
        - remove

      else
        marker.update-coordinates
  else
    * no marker for this new user we dont have in the stack
    - add new marker and store it



current gps logic
- navigatorinit
  true / false
  - > updateuserlocation

updated gps logic

- keep navigatorinit
- get data (gpsFetchStorage)
- remove myself (if found in object)
- display data (displayUsersPosition)

